---
import { readings, scenarios, days } from '../../data/handshake-study.js';
import '../../styles/handshake-study.css';
export const prerender = false;
Astro.response.headers.set('X-Robots-Tag', 'noindex, nofollow, noarchive');
Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', 'private, no-store');
Astro.response.headers.set('Referrer-Policy', 'no-referrer');
const categories = [...new Set(readings.map(r=>r.category))];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow, noarchive"/><meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer"/><title>Min Kim · AI Safety & Evaluation Study</title><meta name="description" content="Independent study notes on AI safety policy, evaluation design and human review operations, prepared by Min Kim."/><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico"/></head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header class="topbar"><a class="wordmark" href="#top">Min Kim<span>STUDY PORTFOLIO</span></a><nav aria-label="Study sections"><a href="#readings">Reading notes</a><a href="#lab">Evaluation lab</a><a href="#operations">Operations</a><a href="#plan">Study plan</a></nav><span class="pill">Independent study</span></header>
<main id="main">
<section class="hero" id="top"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> PREPARED FOR A CONVERSATION ABOUT HANDSHAKE AI</div><h1>Human judgment.<br/><span>Measurable AI quality.</span></h1><p class="intro">A study notebook on translating safety policy into clear evaluation criteria, reliable human review and accountable delivery.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="#readings">Explore the study notes <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#lab">Try the evaluation lab ↓</a></div><div class="hero-bottom"><span>MIN KIM / AI GOVERNANCE</span><span>Sources reviewed · October 19, 2026</span></div></section>
<section class="context wrap"><p class="label">THE THROUGH-LINE</p><h2>From a policy principle<br/>to a defensible decision.</h2><ol class="pipeline">{[['01','Understand','The company and the work'],['02','Interpret','Rules, context and exceptions'],['03','Design','Cases and measurable criteria'],['04','Calibrate','Labels, feedback and review'],['05','Operate','Quality, time and cost']].map(([n,t,d])=><li><span>{n}</span><strong>{t}</strong><p>{d}</p></li>)}</ol><p class="notice">An independent preparation project by Min Kim, inspired by Handshake AI’s visual style. These are summaries and proposed applications of public materials—not Handshake training, internal procedures or an endorsed assessment. The job posting itself was not supplied, so role-specific assumptions need confirmation.</p></section>
<section class="section wrap" id="readings"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="label">01 / READING NOTES</p><h2>Eight sources.<br/>One operational perspective.</h2></div><p>For each reading: the concept, an example and the action I would take. Read the original for full conditions and updates.</p></div><div class="filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter readings"><button class="active" data-filter="All" aria-pressed="true">All readings</button>{categories.map(c=><button data-filter={c} aria-pressed="false">{c}</button>)}</div><p id="reading-count" class="small" role="status">8 reading notes</p><div class="reading-grid">{readings.map(r=><article class="reading-card" data-category={r.category}><div class="card-top"><span>{r.number} / {r.category}</span><span>{r.time}</span></div><h3>{r.title}</h3><p>{r.summary}</p><ol class="mini-flow" aria-label={`${r.title} conceptual flow`}>{r.map.map(m=><li>{m}</li>)}</ol><div class="takeaway"><span>KEY TAKEAWAY</span><strong>{r.takeaway}</strong></div><details><summary>Example, application & discussion question <span>+</span></summary><dl><dt>Illustrative example</dt><dd>{r.example}</dd><dt>How I would apply it</dt><dd>{r.action}</dd><dt>Question to discuss</dt><dd>{r.question}</dd></dl><p class="small">{r.limit}</p></details><footer><a href={r.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{r.publisher} ↗</a>{r.second&&<a href={r.second} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AI Trainer workflow guide ↗</a>}</footer></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="policy-band"><div class="wrap"><p class="label">A DISTINCTION I WOULD MAKE EARLY</p><h2>Three documents.<br/>Three different questions.</h2><div class="three-grid">{[['Model behavior standard','How should the assistant respond?','Example: a boundary and its contextual exceptions.'],['Service usage policy','What uses of the service are permitted?','Example: a restricted application or activity.'],['Project evaluation rubric','How should this item be labeled?','Example: label definitions, evidence and escalation rules.']].map(([t,q,e])=><article><span class="rule-line"></span><h3>{t}</h3><p>{q}</p><small>{e}</small></article>)}</div><p class="band-note">My proposed workflow: identify the governing document → record its version → map it to the rubric → escalate unresolved interpretation. A study example does not override a project’s authorized policy.</p></div></section>
<section class="section wrap" id="lab"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="label">02 / INTERACTIVE EVALUATION LAB</p><h2>99% accurate.<br/>Still missing every violation.</h2></div><p>Explore the supplied 1,000-case example. “Violation” is the positive class. All values are synthetic, not company results.</p></div><div class="lab-grid"><div class="lab-controls"><h3>Change the reviewer’s classifications</h3><p>Reference labels: <b>10 violations</b> and <b>990 allowed cases</b>.</p><label for="tp">Violations correctly caught <output id="tp-value">0 / 10</output></label><input type="range" id="tp" min="0" max="10" value="0"/><label for="fp">Allowed cases incorrectly flagged <output id="fp-value">0 / 990</output></label><input type="range" id="fp" min="0" max="990" value="0"/><div class="preset"><button id="all-allowed">Predict all allowed</button><button id="mixed">Try a mixed result</button></div><p class="small">These sliders change counts directly; they are not a model threshold or an empirical ROC curve.</p><a href="https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/crash-course/classification/accuracy-precision-recall" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Metric definitions · Google ↗</a></div><div><table class="matrix"><caption>Confusion matrix · counts</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Reference ↓ / prediction →</th><th scope="col">Violation</th><th scope="col">Allowed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Violation</th><td class="correct"><span>True positive</span><strong id="tp-cell">0</strong></td><td class="miss"><span>False negative</span><strong id="fn-cell">10</strong></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Allowed</th><td class="miss"><span>False positive</span><strong id="fp-cell">0</strong></td><td class="correct"><span>True negative</span><strong id="tn-cell">990</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><div class="metrics"><div><span>Accuracy</span><strong id="accuracy">99.0%</strong><small>(TP + TN) / all cases</small></div><div><span>Precision</span><strong id="precision">N/A</strong><small>TP / (TP + FP)</small></div><div><span>Recall</span><strong id="recall">0.0%</strong><small>TP / (TP + FN)</small></div></div><p id="metric-story" class="insight" aria-live="polite">All 10 violations are missed. High accuracy hides complete failure to identify the positive class. Precision is undefined because nothing was flagged.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section wrap" id="calibration"><p class="label">03 / CALIBRATION WORKBENCH</p><h2>Disagreement is a signal.<br/>Investigate before assigning blame.</h2><div class="calibration-grid"><div><p>Illustrative labels from three reviewers. Each row is one item; the numbers below describe this tiny demonstration only.</p><table class="agreement"><caption>Synthetic review sample</caption><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>A</th><th>B</th><th>C</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>01</th><td>Allow</td><td>Allow</td><td>Allow</td></tr><tr><th>02</th><td>Flag</td><td>Flag</td><td>Flag</td></tr><tr class="split"><th>03</th><td>Allow</td><td>Flag</td><td>Allow</td></tr><tr class="split"><th>04</th><td>Flag</td><td>Allow</td><td>Flag</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="stat-row"><strong>50%<small>unanimous items · 2 / 4</small></strong><strong>66.7%<small>pairwise agreement · 8 / 12</small></strong></div><p class="small">Pairwise agreement counts the three reviewer pairs within each item. This is descriptive agreement, not chance-corrected agreement or accuracy.</p></div><div class="diagnostic"><h3>A proposed diagnostic sequence</h3><ol><li><b>Inspect the case.</b> Check missing context and the exact rule.</li><li><b>Compare rationales.</b> Look for recurring interpretation differences.</li><li><b>Check the version.</b> Ensure reviewers used the same criteria.</li><li><b>Adjudicate.</b> Ask the authorized owner to resolve the boundary.</li><li><b>Recalibrate.</b> Add contrasting examples and review a fresh sample.</li></ol><p>Consensus alone cannot prove correctness. Preserve dissent and uncertainty when the evidence does not support a settled answer.</p><a href={readings[4].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source workflow · Label Studio ↗</a></div></div></section>
<section class="section wrap" id="operations"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="label">04 / OPERATING JUDGMENT</p><h2>What I would do next.</h2></div><p>Five proposed responses to the preparation scenarios. Owners and actions are illustrative; actual authority and procedures must be confirmed.</p></div><div class="scenario-layout"><div class="scenario-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Choose an operating scenario">{scenarios.map((s,i)=><button data-scenario={i} aria-pressed={i===0?'true':'false'} class={i===0?'active':''}><span>0{i+1}</span>{s.title}<span>↗</span></button>)}</div><div>{scenarios.map((s,i)=><article class="scenario-panel" data-panel={i} hidden={i!==0}><span class="pill">PROPOSED RESPONSE</span><h3>{s.title}</h3><dl>{[['Problem',s.problem],['Information to confirm',s.info],['Action',s.action],['Accountable owner',s.owner],['How to verify the result',s.verify]].map(([t,d])=><div><dt>{t}</dt><dd>{d}</dd></div>)}</dl></article>)}</div></div></section>
<section class="section wrap" id="analysis"><p class="label">05 / ANALYTICAL PRACTICE</p><h2>Make the denominator explicit.</h2><div class="two-grid"><div><p>This proposed query compares labels with a finalized reference label, grouped by policy category. The schema assumes one row per task and one final review per task.</p><p>Confirm uniqueness before joining. Exclude unresolved reviews deliberately, report how many were excluded, and avoid interpreting an unreviewed item as a correct one.</p><a href="https://sqlbolt.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Practice the SQL building blocks ↗</a></div><pre aria-label="Illustrative SQL query"><code>{`-- Illustrative schema, not production data.
SELECT t.policy_category,
       COUNT(*) AS reviewed_items,
       SUM(CASE WHEN t.label <> r.reference_label
                THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS errors,
       1.0 * SUM(CASE
         WHEN t.label <> r.reference_label
         THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(*) AS error_rate
FROM tasks t
JOIN final_reviews r ON r.task_id = t.id
WHERE r.status = 'resolved'
  AND t.label IS NOT NULL
  AND r.reference_label IS NOT NULL
  AND t.policy_version = r.policy_version
GROUP BY t.policy_category;`}</code></pre></div></section>
<section class="section wrap" id="plan"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="label">06 / SEVEN-DAY STUDY ROUTE</p><h2>Read. Apply. Explain.</h2></div><p>A preparation plan, not a claim of completed coursework. Each day ends with one concept, one example and one action.</p></div><ol class="days">{days.map(([t,d],i)=><li><span>DAY 0{i+1}</span><h3>{t}</h3><p>{d}</p></li>)}</ol><div class="closing"><h3>The question I want to answer well</h3><p>“When judgments diverge, how do we find the cause, improve the guidance and demonstrate that quality improved?”</p><a class="button" href="#readings">Return to the evidence ↑</a></div></section>
</main>
<footer class="site-footer wrap"><div><strong>Min Kim</strong><p>Independent AI safety & evaluation study portfolio.</p></div><div><p>Direct-link page · excluded from site navigation and search.</p><p>Anyone with this URL can view it. It is not password-protected.</p><p>Public sources reviewed October 19, 2026. Summaries and examples may need revision as sources change.</p></div></footer>
<script>
 const buttons=document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-filter]');
 buttons.forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>{let count=0;document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-category]').forEach(card=>{card.hidden=button.dataset.filter!=='All'&&card.dataset.category!==button.dataset.filter;if(!card.hidden)count++;});buttons.forEach(b=>{const on=b===button;b.classList.toggle('active',on);b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(on));});document.getElementById('reading-count')!.textContent=`${count} reading ${count===1?'note':'notes'}`;}));
 const tp=document.getElementById('tp') as HTMLInputElement,fp=document.getElementById('fp') as HTMLInputElement;
 const put=(id:string,text:string)=>{document.getElementById(id)!.textContent=text;};
 function update(){const t=Number(tp.value),f=Number(fp.value),fn=10-t,tn=990-f;put('tp-value',`${t} / 10`);put('fp-value',`${f} / 990`);put('tp-cell',String(t));put('fp-cell',String(f));put('fn-cell',String(fn));put('tn-cell',String(tn));put('accuracy',((t+tn)/10).toFixed(1)+'%');put('precision',t+f?((t/(t+f))*100).toFixed(1)+'%':'N/A');put('recall',(t*10).toFixed(1)+'%');put('metric-story',t===0&&f===0?'All 10 violations are missed. High accuracy hides complete failure to identify the positive class. Precision is undefined because nothing was flagged.':`${t} of 10 violations caught; ${fn} missed. ${f} allowed cases incorrectly flagged. Review severity and category-level results before drawing a quality conclusion.`);}
 tp.addEventListener('input',update);fp.addEventListener('input',update);document.getElementById('all-allowed')!.addEventListener('click',()=>{tp.value='0';fp.value='0';update();});document.getElementById('mixed')!.addEventListener('click',()=>{tp.value='8';fp.value='20';update();});
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-scenario]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>{document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-panel]').forEach(panel=>panel.hidden=panel.dataset.panel!==button.dataset.scenario);document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-scenario]').forEach(b=>{const on=b===button;b.classList.toggle('active',on);b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(on));});}));
</script>
</body></html>
